.TH host_info 1 3/25/87
.CM 4
.SH NAME
.nf
hostinfo \- display information about a Mach host
.SH SYNOPSIS
hostinfo
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.I hostinfo
program displays information about a Mach host.  In particular, it displays
the maximum number of processors the kernel was configured for, the actual
number of processors physically available in the hardware
configuration, and the amount of physical memory available in the host.
Then, for each logical slot,
.I hostinfo
displays information about the processor configured in that slot.  The
information includes the slot number, the cpu type and sub-type, whether or
not the processor is executing, and finally, a summary of the processor
utilization since boot time.  The processor utilization is split into user,
system and idle time.

The information provided by this program should be expanded in the future.
In addition, it should be possible to query other hosts in the network in
future versions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I host_info(2), slot_info(2), slot_name(3)
